    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build is green. Here's what I implemented.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec asks for `riskFlag` on an owner to be `true` when any of three signals hold. Two of those signals already existed in the create pipeline as stored owner state; the third (\"disposable-adjacent\" email) was new. I kept each piece in its natural home rather than growing a catch-all.\n\n**1. `OwnerEmails` \u2014 the email rule set (`rest/function/owner/OwnerEmails.java`)**\nAdded `isDisposableAdjacent(email)`: a domain that shares a known disposable provider's second-level label (e.g. `mailinator.net`, `sub.mailinator.com`) without being an outright disposable domain (those are already rejected 400 at create, so a *stored* email is never fully disposable \u2014 adjacency is the meaningful signal here). The adjacent-label set is derived from the existing `DISPOSABLE_DOMAINS` so the two never drift. Promoted the class to `public` (matching the sibling `OwnerTelephones`, already used cross-package by the mapper).\n\n**2. `OwnerMapper` \u2014 the derived response fields (`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`)**\nAdded a small `riskFlag(owner)` method that ORs the three signals, reusing what already exists:\n- possible duplicate \u2192 the existing `possibleDuplicate(owner)` (`possibleDuplicateOf != null`)\n- city over soft capacity \u2192 the stored `capacityWarning` flag (set at creation by `AssignOwnerCapacityWarning` for cities holding 40\u201349 owners)\n- disposable-adjacent email \u2192 `OwnerEmails.isDisposableAdjacent`\n\n`riskFlag` is a pure derived field like `possibleDuplicate` \u2014 computed at mapping time, no new DB column.\n\n**3. `openapi.yml`** \u2014 declared `riskFlag` as a `readOnly` boolean on the `Owner` schema (DTOs are generated from this spec at build), so it serializes as `$.riskFlag`.\n\nThe acceptance test (`coreRiskFlagFalseNormally`, which creates a clean owner \u2014 no duplicate, no email, unique city \u2014 and asserts `riskFlag` is `false`) passes, as does the full suite (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
